---
/* L93 - the package: four parts, assembled in order, evidence before the claim. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L93.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of an open box of papers and a notebook being handed across a table from one pair of hands to another."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L93-fig-title L93-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L93-fig-title">The four parts of the package, and the rule that the evidence comes first</title>
      <desc id="L93-fig-desc">
        Four slabs stacked down the page, numbered one to four and joined by a
        prussian line that draws itself downward. One, the repo: pure standard
        library, no install step, Apache-2.0. Two, the command: one line to type,
        the environment variable it needs, well under a dollar. Three, the raw
        evidence: the .jsonl, the .meta.json and the derived .md, with the run id,
        the battery hash and the uuid. Four, one finding: one checkable sentence,
        with its status label and its limitations. Below: the review before
        publishing, the mock labelled as a mock, and the raw files append-only.
      </desc>

      <!-- 1 the repo -->
      <rect
        class="m-fade"
        style="--m-duration: 0.7s; --m-delay: 0.15s;"
        x="30" y="50" width="580" height="44"
        fill="var(--color-ground)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1"
      />
      <text x="42" y="76" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">1</text>
      <text x="78" y="76" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink)">the repo</text>
      <text x="200" y="70" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">pure standard library, no install step</text>
      <text x="200" y="86" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">Apache-2.0</text>

      <!-- 2 the command -->
      <rect
        class="m-fade"
        style="--m-duration: 0.7s; --m-delay: 0.4s;"
        x="30" y="104" width="580" height="44"
        fill="var(--color-ground)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1"
      />
      <text x="42" y="130" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">2</text>
      <text x="78" y="130" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink)">the command</text>
      <text x="200" y="124" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">one line to type, the environment variable it needs</text>
      <text x="200" y="140" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">well under $1</text>

      <!-- 3 the raw evidence -->
      <rect
        class="m-fade"
        style="--m-duration: 0.7s; --m-delay: 0.65s;"
        x="30" y="158" width="580" height="44"
        fill="var(--color-ground)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1"
      />
      <text x="42" y="184" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">3</text>
      <text x="78" y="184" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink)">the raw evidence</text>
      <text x="200" y="178" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">the .jsonl, the .meta.json, the derived .md</text>
      <text x="200" y="194" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">run id, battery_hash, uuid</text>

      <!-- 4 one finding -->
      <rect
        class="m-fade"
        style="--m-duration: 0.7s; --m-delay: 0.9s;"
        x="30" y="212" width="580" height="44"
        fill="var(--color-ground)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1"
      />
      <text x="42" y="238" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">4</text>
      <text x="78" y="238" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink)">one finding</text>
      <text x="200" y="232" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">one checkable sentence</text>
      <text x="200" y="248" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">with its status label and its limitations</text>

      <!-- the spine: the package is assembled in order -->
      <path
        class="m-draw"
        style="--m-length: 200; --m-duration: 1.4s;"
        d="M 62 58 V 250"
        fill="none"
        stroke="var(--color-prussian)"
        stroke-width="1"
      />
      <line x1="62" y1="72" x2="70" y2="72" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="62" y1="126" x2="70" y2="126" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="62" y1="180" x2="70" y2="180" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="62" y1="234" x2="70" y2="234" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />

      <text x="30" y="284" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">the review before you publish: 5 minutes, 7 checks</text>
      <text x="30" y="304" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">the mock is labelled as a mock, in the banner and in the write-up</text>
      <text x="30" y="324" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">the raw files are append-only: never edited, never deleted</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L93</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">The repo, the command, the raw evidence and the one finding - assembled in that order, so the reader can check the last one against the third.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  /* scoped to this figure */
  .fig__svg {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
